            "curator": "all-unmatched-20261107-worker07-root",
            "action": "CORRECT_ISOLATED_PROPOSAL_EVIDENCE",
            "changes": "Issue1226: Reclassify only ontology_mapping.evidence indices 0 from MANUAL_CURATION to LLM_SUGGESTION. Exact complete objects were rebound to the frozen provenance audit; these entries record documented agent interpretation, not human-supplied evidence. Sources, claim notes and historical entries are retained; ComponentEvidenceTypeEnum and canonical SSSOM ManualMappingCuration are unchanged. Issue1237 W01-PREP-B-001: NBRC1507 names 0.1 M Tris/HCl (pH7.5) as a supplied buffer. It does not enumerate free hydrochloric acid as a separately added component. Retain the named buffer moiety and nominal strength; the complete constituent list, solvent, preparation and neutralization ratio remain unknown. No dry Tris-HCl substitution or neutralization chemistry is inferred. Remove the unsupported separate Hydrochloric acid has-part assertion; preserve UNKNOWN completeness and the first named buffer moiety at 0.1 M. Isolated report-only successor; no owner, role, source gate or release approval.",
            "llm_assisted": true
          }
        },
        {
          "path": "/notes",
          "before": "Source specifies0.1M Tris/HCl,pH7.5; nominal total Tris moiety concentration retained, not independent concentrations for acid and conjugate base. Solvent and neutralization ratio unreported. Raw assigned source label: 0.1 M Tris/HCl (pH7.5). Quantities in notes preserve source preparation and are not final-medium concentrations. No global synonym is added for this context-dependent label.",
          "after": "Source specifies0.1M Tris/HCl,pH7.5; nominal total Tris moiety concentration retained, not independent concentrations for acid and conjugate base. Solvent and neutralization ratio unreported. Raw assigned source label: 0.1 M Tris/HCl (pH7.5). Quantities in notes preserve source preparation and are not final-medium concentrations. No global synonym is added for this context-dependent label. Issue1237 W01-PREP-B-001: NBRC1507 names 0.1 M Tris/HCl (pH7.5) as a supplied buffer. It does not enumerate free hydrochloric acid as a separately added component. Retain the named buffer moiety and nominal strength; the complete constituent list, solvent, preparation and neutralization ratio remain unknown. No dry Tris-HCl substitution or neutralization chemistry is inferred."
        },
        {
          "path": "/ontology_mapping/evidence/0/evidence_type",
          "before": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "after": "LLM_SUGGESTION"
        }
      ],
      "source_assessment": "NBRC1507 and TOGO M2152 identify the named 0.1 M Tris/HCl pH7.5 buffer as a 50 mL receiving-medium addition; neither supplies a stock recipe or free acid input. Remove only unsupported Hydrochloric acid part. Preserve Tris named moiety 0.1 M, pH7.5 and UNKNOWN constituent completeness.",
