      "all_changed_paths": [
        {
          "path": "/curation_history/3",
          "before_missing": true,
          "after": {
            "timestamp": "2026-11-08T07:39:32.315188+00:00",
            "curator": "all-unmatched-20261107-worker07-root",
            "action": "CORRECT_ISOLATED_PROPOSAL_EVIDENCE",
            "changes": "Issue1226: Reclassify only ontology_mapping.evidence indices 0,1 from MANUAL_CURATION to LLM_SUGGESTION. Exact complete objects were rebound to the frozen provenance audit; these entries record documented agent interpretation, not human-supplied evidence. Sources, claim notes and historical entries are retained; ComponentEvidenceTypeEnum and canonical SSSOM ManualMappingCuration are unchanged. Issue1237 MIN-F02: Comparison with DSM590/1144 remains unresolved at complete chemical/preparation scope. JCM149 Metals44 prints EDTA·2Na and MnSO4·xH2O; DSM prints Na-EDTA and MnSO4·H2O plus a few drops of concentrated H2SO4. Unspecified hydration, salt detail or an unreported acid step does not prove incompatibility or equivalence. The historical malformed molybdate strings remain literal unresolved assertions. Positively different JCM149 outer Hutner mineral base has MgSO4·7H2O 14.45 g versus 29.7 g in JCM900/979; that outer recipe is distinct from the nested Metals44 reference. JCM631 also retains its positively different Mg/Ca quantities and vitamin inputs. All present immediate inputs remain unchanged; COMPLETE is source-list completeness, not resolved molecular identity. Isolated report-only successor; no owner, role, source gate or release approval.",
            "llm_assisted": true
          }
        },
        {
          "path": "/notes",
          "before": "The primary JCM 900 and JCM 979 stock subrecipes specify the same nine named inputs, quantities, Metals 44 reference to JCM 149 and preparation: dissolve NTA, adjust to pH 7.0 with about 7.3 g KOH, add the remaining ingredients, and readjust to pH 6.8 with NaOH or H2SO4. Parent media and vitamin supplements differ outside this stock boundary. The literal malformed (NH4)6MoO24·4H2O remains unresolved; no heptamolybdate correction or exact chemical-component equivalence is asserted. Raw source names Hutner's basal salts (see below) and Modified Hutner's basal salts remain in the frozen case evidence; neither becomes a global stock synonym. The canonical proposed local registry identifier retains JCM 900 provenance and also covers this verified JCM 979 subrecipe.",
          "after": "The primary JCM 900 and JCM 979 stock subrecipes specify the same nine named inputs, quantities, Metals 44 reference to JCM 149 and preparation: dissolve NTA, adjust to pH 7.0 with about 7.3 g KOH, add the remaining ingredients, and readjust to pH 6.8 with NaOH or H2SO4. Parent media and vitamin supplements differ outside this stock boundary. The literal malformed (NH4)6MoO24·4H2O remains unresolved; no heptamolybdate correction or exact chemical-component equivalence is asserted. Raw source names Hutner's basal salts (see below) and Modified Hutner's basal salts remain in the frozen case evidence; neither becomes a global stock synonym. The canonical proposed local registry identifier retains JCM 900 provenance and also covers this verified JCM 979 subrecipe. Issue1237 MIN-F02: Comparison with DSM590/1144 remains unresolved at complete chemical/preparation scope. JCM149 Metals44 prints EDTA·2Na and MnSO4·xH2O; DSM prints Na-EDTA and MnSO4·H2O plus a few drops of concentrated H2SO4. Unspecified hydration, salt detail or an unreported acid step does not prove incompatibility or equivalence. The historical malformed molybdate strings remain literal unresolved assertions. Positively different JCM149 outer Hutner mineral base has MgSO4·7H2O 14.45 g versus 29.7 g in JCM900/979; that outer recipe is distinct from the nested Metals44 reference. JCM631 also retains its positively different Mg/Ca quantities and vitamin inputs. All present immediate inputs remain unchanged; COMPLETE is source-list completeness, not resolved molecular identity."
        },
        {
          "path": "/ontology_mapping/evidence/0/evidence_type",
          "before": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "after": "LLM_SUGGESTION"
        },
        {
          "path": "/ontology_mapping/evidence/1/evidence_type",
          "before": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "after": "LLM_SUGGESTION"
        }
      ],
      "source_assessment": "JCM900 and979 outer stock immediate lists and process match, including NTA10g, MgSO4 heptahydrate29.7g, CaCl2 dihydrate3.335g, molybdate literal9.25mg, FeSO4 heptahydrate99mg, Metals44(JCM149)50mL, water950mL, about7.3gKOH/pH7 and laterNaOH-or-H2SO4/pH6.8. Relative to DSM counterparts, nested EDTA/Mn hydration/acid-step details are unresolved, not proof of incompatibility. JCM149 outer Mg14.45g rather than29.7g is a positive difference; JCM631 Mg14.45g/Ca4.42g and vitamins also differ positively.",
      "remaining_holds": "Malformed JCM molybdate; JCM149 nested EDTA·2Na hydration and MnSO4·xH2O; relationship to DSM Na-EDTA/MnSO4·H2O and whether omitted nested acid processing is common or differs. Preserve COMPLETE immediate list separately from unresolved molecular grounding; no JCM/DSM owner union approved.",
      "scientific_delta_verdict": "pass_with_limitations",
      "whole_owner_or_release_approval": false
    }
  ],
